{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_018SUFW9XqdBr9EJVwCj5vUL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote **`answers/07-009-multi-layer-caching-retrieval-prompt-response.md`** — Q9: Multi-layer caching: retrieval, prompt, response?\n\nThe note covers the three-layer architecture:\n\n| Layer | Mechanism | Hit rate | Savings |\n|-------|-----------|----------|---------|\n| **L3 Response cache** | GPTCache / Redis-FAISS, cosine > 0.93, semantic similarity gate | 20–35% | Entire LLM call skipped |\n| **L2 Prefix cache** | Provider-side KV cache on static system prompt (Anthropic/OpenAI), 90% discount on cached tokens | 50–90% on static prefix | Major input-token cost cut |\n| **L1 Retrieval cache** | SHA-256 hash → skip embed API; cosine-gated Redis TTL → skip ANN search | 15–40% | Embedding + retrieval skipped |\n\nKey pitfalls flagged: treating it as a single-layer problem, setting cosine threshold too low causing false-positive cache hits (the \"cancel vs pause subscription\" example), and using only TTL instead of namespace-scoped webhook-triggered invalidation on content updates. The concrete math shows a 62% cost reduction at 1M queries/day."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":291,"cache_read_input_tokens":72961,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":291,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce8bd693-0d62-4128-8b64-0f025cb98e31","uuid":"4f6b03a7-5226-419c-819f-426b5faccbdc"}
